# Milestone: M3 (updated v0.10.9-tag-state W2: D3 outside-scope fatal)
# Covers: TAG_STOP is not intercepted by a try/catch block; the catch clause
#         is skipped and TAG_STOP continues propagating outward.
#
# Activated: v0.10.7 W7 — Tag.new() + tag.stop() shipped (v0.10.2 W4).
# Old label: T29
#
# Semantics: the unwind walker absorbs UEXEC_THROW in UCLEANUP_TRY_FRAME but
# does NOT absorb UEXEC_TAG_STOP; TAG_STOP propagates past catch clauses.
# `Realm.caught` remains 0 confirming catch was not executed.
#
# v0.10.9-tag-state W2: TAG_STOP propagation past catch now ALSO triggers the
# D3 outside-scope fatal because the syntactic `t:` scope creates an anonymous
# UTag, not one bound to `t` (bare-prefix tag-label binding is deferred-v1.x).
# So `t.stop()` is "outside any active scope for t" — escalates to fatal,
# emitting `!!!`.  Catch is still skipped (`Realm.caught` stays 0); the test
# now also confirms the D3 fatal path.  Workspace-root compatibility-decisions
# ledger §S5c.

var t = Tag.new()
var caught = 0
t: { try { t.stop() } catch (e) { Realm.caught = 1 } }
Realm.caught
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] !!! tag.stop with no active scope
[00000001] 0
